{{Quote|A Wookiee! Rare you are to the Jedi. Proud, your people must be.|Professor Huyang to Gungi|<ref name="ATS">{{TCW|A Test of Strength}}</ref>}}
'''Gungi''' was a [[Gender|male]] [[Wookiee]] [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] who [[Jedi training|trained]] to become a Jedi in the [[Jedi Order]] during the [[Republic Era|era]] of the [[Galactic Republic]]. During the [[Clone Wars]], Gungi and a group of five other younglings, [[Petro]], [[Katooni]], [[Byph]], [[Ganodi]], and [[Zatt]], were deemed to be at the top of their class and, led by [[Ahsoka Tano]] and Jedi Grand Master Yoda, they traveled to [[Ilum]] to participate in [[Gathering|the Gathering]]; an ancient Jedi ritual that proved a [[youngling]]'s readiness to become a Padawan. Gungi managed to survive the [[Great Jedi Purge]] and continued acting as a Jedi during the early [[Imperial Era|reign]] of the [[Galactic Empire]].

==Biography==
===Serving the Jedi Order===
====The Gathering====
[[File:Epguide506.jpg|thumb|left|290px|Gungi preparing to leave Coruscant]]
Gungi, a [[Gender|male]] [[Wookiee]] who was among the top of his class, was sent to [[Ilum]] with five of his fellow [[Jedi]] [[Jedi Initiate|younglings]]. While on Ilum, the [[youngling]]s were instructed by [[Jedi Master]] [[Yoda]] to enter a [[Crystal Cave]] and find their [[kyber crystal]]s, which were necessary for the younglings to construct their first [[lightsaber]]s. Every [[crystal]] in the cave was specific to each individual. Gungi found his crystal on an island across a body of [[water]] within the cave. Following [[Ganodi]]'s advice not go into the freezing water, he meditated to wait for the body of water to freeze so he could cross. He was later commended by Master Yoda on his patience.<ref name="TCW:TG" />

====Captured by pirates====
While on their way back to [[Coruscant]] aboard the ''[[Crucible]]'', Gungi and his fellow younglings began creating their lightsabers under the guidance of [[Professor]] [[Huyang]] when the Jedi's [[Starship|ship]] was [[Raid on the Crucible|attacked]] by the [[pirate]] [[Hondo Ohnaka]]. Hondo and his pirate [[Ohnaka Gang|crew]] were looking for the kyber crystals the younglings had just collected as they were worth lots of [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]] on the [[black market]]. All the younglings gave Huyang their crystals, except [[Petro]], who gave a droid component instead. Soon after, several of Ohnaka's pirates found Gungi, Huyang, [[Katooni]] and Petro hiding in the ventilation system. Petro revealed his improperly constructed [[Petro's lightsaber|lightsaber]]. The saber's [[emitter matrix]] caused the saber to explode, incapacitating the pirates, in turn allowing Gungi, Huyang and the other younglings to escape from the pirates. Although the younglings managed to repel the pirates, [[Ahsoka Tano]] was pulled into [[Realspace|space]] along with the pirates because the ''Crucible'' had managed to get away from the pirates docking station and had created a vacuum.<ref name="ATS" />

[[File:AnimalInstincts-BFR.png|thumb|right|290px|Gungi and the younglings posing as a circus act to rescue Ahsoka]]
Gungi and his youngling friends were building their lightsabers as they had free time, due to the fact their ship was stranded. After Gungi, Petro, and [[Byph]] finished their lightsabers the group decided to go to [[Florrum]] to cool their engines (which were at risk of exploding) and to save Ahsoka. Once there, they joined the [[Preigo's Traveling World of Wonder|troupe]] of the [[Dug]] [[Preigo]] to infiltrate the [[Hondo's complex|base]] of Hondo before stealing back [[Ahsoka Tano's lightsabers|Ahsoka's lightsabers]], [[Rescue on Florrum|freeing]] Ahsoka and escaping on a stolen [[speeder]].<ref name="ANB">{{TCW|A Necessary Bond}}</ref>

====Battle against Grievous====
[[File:StandingUpToGrievous-ANB.png|thumb|left|250px|Gungi and his friends draw their lightsabers.]]
After escaping on the stolen speeder, Petro made contact with [[R2-D2]] and Ganodi on board the ''Crucible'', but by the time the ''Crucible'' got to them, the speeder was almost at a ravine. The Jedi had to attempt to board the ship hurriedly, with Gungi and Byph hanging off of the edge of the boarding ramp before the pirates shot a missile at the ship, causing it to crash and the pirates to take them hostage yet again. When they reached Hondo's base they found it was under [[Invasion of Florrum|attack]] by [[General]] [[Grievous]] and with the common goal to escape the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatists]], the Jedi and the pirates worked together freeing Ohnaka and escaped to his secret private fleet before managing to leave Florrum.<ref name="Bound for Rescue" />

====Bombing at the Temple====
Gungi was later seen training outside the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] some [[time]] after the [[Bombing of the Jedi Temple hangar|bombing]] of the Temple's [[hangar]]. Along with his [[teacher]], [[Tera Sinube]], Gungi observed as [[Anakin Skywalker]] and [[Barriss Offee]] [[Duel at the Jedi Temple|dueled]] outside until Offee was apprehended.<ref name="TWJ">{{TCW|The Wrong Jedi}}</ref>

===Great Jedi Purge===
====Rescue====
[[File:Gungi_lightsaber_TBBS2.png|thumb|right|290px|Gungi reclaims his lightsaber from the Axis droids.]]
Gungi, who attained the rank of Padawan,<ref name="Kashyyyk">{{Databank|kashyyyk|Kashyyyk}}</ref> managed to survive the [[Great Jedi Purge]] and kept acting as a Jedi during the early [[Imperial Era]].<ref name="Tribe" /> By [[18 BBY]],<ref name="18 BBY Date">{{TBBDate|206}}</ref> Gungi had been captured by the droids of the [[Vanguard Axis]] and taken prisoner in their [[Axis Base|base]] on board their [[Ordo Tera Spaceport|space station]]. He was kept there while the Axis arranged for him to be sold alive to a wealthy buyer, with their leader keeping Gungi's lightsaber on him at all times. At some point, he was able to escape his cell but was caught by two droids who electrocuted him with a [[electrostaff]]. [[Omega]], a female [[clone]] of [[Jango Fett]] who was present at the station along with [[Clone Force 99]] to sell forged [[chain code]]s to the Axis, caught up to Gungi's torturers and shot them with [[Omega's Zygerrian energy bow|her]] [[energy bow]], freeing him. Gungi and Omega were joined by the rest of Clone Force 99, who engaged the other droids and rescued Gungi aboard their [[Omicron-class attack shuttle|''Omicron''-class attack shuttle]], the [[Marauder (Omicron-class)|''Marauder'']].<ref name="Tribe" />

Distraught by the experience, Gungi stayed away from the others as they were traveling away from the station. Omega approached him with a [[Foodstuff|ration pack]] and tried to get him to eat, explaining that her friends might've been clones, but they were no longer working for the [[Galactic Empire]]. Using [[Tech]] as a translator, the Bad Batch was able to convince Gungi of their good intentions and, prompted by Omega, took course for his homeworld of [[Kashyyyk]].<ref name="Tribe" />

====Helping Yanna's tribe====
Upon arriving on Kashyyyk, Force 99 decided to land next to a remote village to avoid being detected by Imperial units possibly patrolling the world. They walked with Gungi through a thick [[forest]] but soon found themselves surrounded by [[Kinrath|netcasters]], whose nest [[Wrecker]] had disrupted in an attempt to clear a path for the team. The netcasters threatened the team brandishing their fangs, but Gungi asked the team to lower their [[blaster]]s and opened himself to the creatures through the Force, showing his and his friends' non-threatening intentions. The netcasters recognized Gungi's connection and allowed them to pass.<ref name="Tribe" />

[[File:OmegaGungi.png|thumb|left|280px|Omega and Gungi fighting against the Trandoshans]]
After successfully navigating through the forest, the group reached the village but found it burning. [[Hunter]] discovered a group of [[Trandoshan]]s in the ruins, and warned the others that they were holding one of the village's Wookiee warriors captive. Enraged, Gungi activated his lightsaber and rushed to the hunters to free his fellow Wookiee. He managed to free him from his handcuffs, but the remaining hunters turned against him with a pair of [[incinerator tank]]s. The Bad Batch joined Gungi and with his help took down the [[tank]]s. As Gungi was mourning the loss of his people in the still burning ruins, the Wookiee warrior who had escaped returned to help with two of his fellow tribesmen riding [[Mylaya]]s. Finding the Trandoshans dead and Gungi in distress, they invited him and his friends to their own [[Wookiee sanctuary|village]]. There, they introduced Gungi to the village elder, [[Yanna]], who was happy to see one of the "planet's youth" returning home. She explained to Gungi and the Batch that the Trandoshans were working for the Empire and helping extract the land's riches. Upon hearing that, an infuriated Gungi slammed his fist on the table, prompting Hunter to vow that he and his team would do everything they could to help [[Yanna's clan|Yanna's tribe]].<ref name="Tribe" />

Meanwhile, the Trandoshans and a group of [[stormtrooper]] clones, led by [[Babwa Venomor]], discovered the remains of his fellow hunters' tanks and realizing that they had been destroyed by use of a lightsaber, he ordered his hunters to raze the jungle to its roots and find the one responsible. His hunters celebrated and began burning the jungle using their incinerator tanks. The flames were visible from the village, where Hunter noticed them through his [[binoculars]] and warned his team. At the same time, Gungi followed Yanna and her warriors to the base of a [[Wroshyr]] [[tree]], where he observed them kneeling and bowing their heads against the wood to ask the trees for their wisdom. Despite being uneducated on his species' culture due to his absence in Coruscant from a very early age, Gungi was soon able to connect with the trees and listen to their will. He soon informed Hunter and the Batch that they (the trees) had an idea; Hunter reluctantly agreed to follow their plan.<ref name="Tribe" />

The Trandoshan convoy made their way through the jungle towards a clearing near Yanna's village; there, they were ambushed by the Wookiees and the batch who were hiding in the bushes. Upon drawing their fire, the teams strategically retreated to make the Trandoshans follow them inside the netcaster nests. As they were getting deeper into the jungle, the Wookiees were able to take down the tanks one by one, although they suffered casualties of their own. Eventually, the Trandoshans were taken down by the warriors and the furious netcasters whose nests had been destroyed by the tanks; Venomor, however, ran away into the jungle following Gungi into another clearing further from the netcaster nests which he set on fire to trap the Wookiee. Gungi was however able to distract the hunter, causing him to surround himself with a ring of fire; trapped in a close-quarters fight Venomor's [[Flame cannon|flamethrower]] was sliced by Gungi's saber, leaving him vulnerable to netcasters who descended from the tress, wrapped him in their webs and carried him to the treetops where he was killed.<ref name="Tribe" />

With the village liberated, Gungi decided to join Yanna's tribe, staying behind to protect his homeworld and defend his people.<ref name="Tribe" />

==Personality and traits==
[[File:Gungi-SWE.png|thumb|right|250px|Gungi struggled with patience and constructed a green-bladed lightsaber.]]
Gungi was a male Wookiee who was 1.53 [[meter]]s, or 5 [[Foot|ft]] tall,<ref name="Join the Battle" /> with [[Color|brown]] [[hair]] and brown [[eye]]s. Gungi, like many other Wookiees, was temperamental and expressive.<ref name="TCW:TG" /> He was also impulsive and aggressive.<ref name="Join the Battle" /> During his trial at the Gathering, he struggled with the concept of patience, and was only able to acquire his kyber crystal after allowing himself to slow down.<ref name="TCW:TG" /> Once he learned he had to slow down, Gungi was able to overcome his flaws and reach his full potential as a member of the [[Jedi Order]].<ref name="Join the Battle" />

==Powers and abilities==
As a Jedi Initiate, Gungi was [[force-sensitive]]<ref name="Join the Battle" /> and skilled in [[telekinesis]]<ref name="ANB" /> and lightsaber combat.<ref name="Join the Battle" />

==Equipment==
Gungi constructed a green-bladed [[Gungi's lightsaber|lightsaber]] of his own with a wooden hilt, made from [[Brylark tree|Brylark wood]], that he chose from amongst the ''Crucible''{{'s}} stores of materials.<ref name="ATS" />

==Behind the scenes==
Gungi first appeared in the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' episode "[[The Gathering (episode)|The Gathering]]," the sixth episode of the [[The Clone Wars: Season Five|fifth season]] of the animated series, released in [[2012]].<ref name="TCW:TG" /> The character's asset was illustrated by [[JP Balmet]]<ref name="EG">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/the-gathering-episode-guide|text="The Gathering" Episode Guide &#124; The Clone Wars}}</ref> and finished on [[February 3]], [[2011]]. The model was sourced in parts from the one of fellow Wookiee [[Chewbacca]].<ref name="Tumblr">{{Tumblr|subdomain=starwars|name=''Star Wars''|url=post/88703944928/concept-for-the-wookiee-jedi-trainee-gungi|text=Concept for the Wookiee Jedi trainee, Gungi.|archivedate=20181218165148}}</ref>

